# Copy this file to `deploy/.env` and replace the placeholders with real values.
# `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is committed.
#
# Both the local Fastify server (`npm run server`) and docker-compose
# (`cd deploy && docker compose up`) pick this file up automatically.

# ─── View-mode quality grid ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate a fresh key with:   openssl rand -hex 32
QUALITY_API_KEY=<64-hex-string>

# ─── LLM proxy (v10.131, Phase L1) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The SPA no longer calls LLM providers directly. All chat requests go
# through `POST /api/llm/chat` on this Fastify server, which then talks to
# the GWM LLM proxy. The same api_key authorizes both LLM and MCP services.

# OpenAI-compatible base URL of the GWM proxy. Defaults to the production
# value if unset. Override only when testing against a different endpoint.
LLMPROXY_BASE_URL=https://llmproxy.gwm.cn/v1

# The api_key the GWM proxy expects. Provisioned by GWM IT — same key works
# for both LLM completions and MCP tool calls. Without this, /api/llm/chat
# will return 502 from the upstream call.
LLMPROXY_API_KEY=<your-llmproxy-key>

# TLS to the proxy. The Node server ships its own CA bundle and may NOT trust a
# corporate proxy cert that your browser trusts — symptom: Task (browser) works
# but Explore (server) fails with "Connection error.".
#   • PROD-correct: make Node trust the corporate root CA. Set this in the REAL
#     environment BEFORE the server starts (read at Node startup, so it can't
#     come from this --env-file): NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/corp-root-ca.pem
#   • DEV-only quick unblock: skip TLS verification (INSECURE — never in prod):
# LLMPROXY_INSECURE_TLS=true

# Max request body (MB) for the Fastify server. Default 8. Raise if multi-modal
# (image) Explore turns are rejected with 413.
# LLM_BODY_LIMIT_MB=8

# NOTE: Explore mode uses THIS server's LLMPROXY_API_KEY/LLMPROXY_BASE_URL — NOT
# the SPA "LLM Settings" (which power Task mode in the browser). So this key must
# be entitled to the models users select in the Explore composer. If the proxy
# drops the connection with `terminated (UND_ERR_SOCKET)` for a model that works
# in Task, the server key likely isn't entitled to that model.

# Diagnostic: disable MCP tool-binding for Explore (the request then matches a
# plain browser completion). Use to rule tools in/out. Dev/diagnosis only.
# EXPLORE_DISABLE_MCP=true

# Optional internal-shared-secret. If set, /api/llm/chat requires an
# `X-Internal-Token` header matching this value. Useful as a sanity guard on
# intranet deployments. Leave unset in dev to skip the check.
# INTERNAL_API_TOKEN=<random-hex-string>

# ─── MCP tool registry (v10.133, Phase L2) ────────────────────────────────
# Path to the MCP server config consumed by `server/mcp/client.ts` at boot.
# Defaults to `deploy/mcp-servers.json` (committed with `${LLMPROXY_API_KEY}`
# placeholder). Override only if you want to load a different config file —
# e.g. point at a host-mounted file in production. If the file is missing
# or unreachable, MCP is disabled cleanly and Explore mode falls back to
# plain chat.
# MCP_CONFIG_PATH=deploy/mcp-servers.json

# How long initMCP waits for `MultiServerMCPClient.getTools()` to resolve
# at boot before giving up and disabling MCP. Units: ms. Default 5000.
# The SDK has no built-in timeout — without this, a slow or unresponsive
# MCP server blocks Fastify from booting at all. Set lower (e.g. 1) to
# disable MCP fast for diagnosis; raise if your MCP server is legitimately
# slow on first connect.
# MCP_INIT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# ─── Speech-to-text (v10.179, voice dictation) ─────────────────────────────
# POST /api/llm/transcribe forwards recorded composer audio to the GWM
# proxy's faster-whisper (OpenAI-compatible audio API). Reuses
# LLMPROXY_BASE_URL / LLMPROXY_API_KEY / the X-Internal-Token guard /
# LLMPROXY_INSECURE_TLS above — no extra credentials needed.
#
# Path under the base URL. Default audio/translations — the ONLY audio path
# the GWM proxy registers (probed 2026-06-10: audio/transcriptions → 404).
# Despite the OpenAI-convention name it does NOT translate: Chinese speech →
# simplified Chinese text (verified against the real endpoint).
# STT_PATH=audio/translations
# STT_MODEL=default/whisper-large-v3-turbo
#
# Upstream wire format (v10.182). The GWM route is NOT OpenAI-compatible: it
# wants JSON `{ model, audio_url: "data:<mime>;base64,..." }` — a multipart
# upload crashes its JSON parse with a bare 500 (this masqueraded as a broken
# upstream until 2026-06-10). Values:
#   gwm-json          GWM's JSON dialect (default — matches the default base URL)
#   openai-multipart  standard OpenAI audio API (tools/local-stt, Speaches, OpenAI)
# STT_FORMAT=gwm-json
#
# v10.181: STT endpoint is decoupled from the chat proxy. STT_BASE_URL /
# STT_API_KEY default to the LLMPROXY_* values above; override to point STT
# elsewhere while chat stays on GWM. Example — the local faster-whisper
# verification server (see tools/local-stt/README.md), auth-less + standard
# OpenAI dialect:
# STT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8100/v1
# STT_API_KEY=
# STT_FORMAT=openai-multipart
# (empty STT_API_KEY sends no Authorization header; remove all three lines to
# return STT to the GWM proxy.)
#
# NOTE: the mic itself needs a SECURE CONTEXT in the browser (HTTPS or
# localhost). On the plain-HTTP intranet deployment the mic button renders
# disabled with an explanatory tooltip. To enable voice in prod, either serve
# over HTTPS, or for managed Chrome/Edge whitelist the deploy origin via
# chrome://flags/#unsafely-treat-insecure-origin-as-secure or the
# InsecureOriginsAllowedForUrls enterprise policy.

# ─── Activity log (v10.228, Config → Activity) ─────────────────────────────
# Critical actions (team save/unlock, ticket create/update, server start) and
# server warn/error are streamed live (SSE) and persisted to the audit_log
# table in quality.db (the existing /app/data volume — no new volume). All
# optional; defaults shown.
# LOG_LEVEL=info               # pino level; the tap captures warn/error regardless
# LOG_RING_SIZE=500            # in-memory live-tail buffer (entries)
# LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=90        # prune audit_log rows older than this
# LOG_RETENTION_ROWS=5000      # and keep at most this many newest rows
